Project Title:
                DevOps MINI SHELL

PROJECT DESCRIPTION:

THE CHALLENGE​:
• Repetitive DevOps operations often require multiple
commands.​
• Switching between commands and scripts can reduce
productivity.​
• Standard shells provide powerful features, but a focused
learning shell can simplify common workflows.​
• The project should also demonstrate core OS concepts
such as process creation, execution and I/O handling.​

OUR SOLUTION​:

• Develop a mini Linux shell that accepts user commands,
executes programs and provides selected automation
features for common DevOps tasks.​
• Goal: make frequent command-line operations simpler
while demonstrating how a shell interacts with the
operating system.​

EXPECTED OUTCOMES:

A functional mini Linux shell with:​

• Interactive command prompt​

• Command parsing and execution​

• Process creation and synchronization​

• Input/output redirection and selected piping​

• Built-in commands for basic shell operations​

• Automation shortcuts for common DevOps tasks​

Expected result: efficient command-line automation with a clear
demonstration of OS-level process management.
                   
